00:24:59,177 --> 00:25:01,760
if you can only get up two

476
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:04,712
or three points, and now you're seeing a

477
00:25:04,712 --> 00:25:07,295
single print with the ratio, you know,

478
00:25:07,295 --> 00:25:09,140
basically indicating that there's really

479
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:15,782
not much interest up here above this, you know, this 45.5, 46 and above level, you know, then what happens?

480
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:17,860
Again, the market sells off.

481
00:25:19,910 --> 00:25:23,470
So, you know, that's one of the problems with trading with moving averages is

482
00:25:23,470 --> 00:25:24,664
they often, price sort

483
00:25:24,664 --> 00:25:26,455
of will, I mean, it acts

484
00:25:26,455 --> 00:25:28,246
as a magnet, and then once

485
00:25:28,246 --> 00:25:31,828
it's around there, it just really can go sideways on you sometimes.

486
00:25:32,230 --> 00:25:33,730
And, you know, you're going to get chopped up.

487
00:25:34,130 --> 00:25:35,750
As I said, I'm not a big fan of moving averages,

488
00:25:36,030 --> 00:25:42,890
but, you know, you can do some analysis of order flows around them.

489
00:25:43,370 --> 00:25:44,610
So here's a trend line again,

490
00:25:44,910 --> 00:25:54,530
and, you know, it's drawn from the low here. So you got here a couple points, one, two.

491
00:25:54,750 --> 00:25:58,850
So, you know, up here, you know, you're well above the trend line.

492
00:25:58,950 --> 00:25:59,510
You have the high.

493
00:25:59,610 --> 00:26:00,990
Okay, you're looking for a break.

494
00:26:01,170 --> 00:26:02,630
You know, you get the little breakthrough here.

495
00:26:03,070 --> 00:26:07,350
Maybe you're not, you know, you don't want to just sell the trend line breakout.

496
00:26:07,450 --> 00:26:12,450
You want to have a reason to be short once you break the trend line, and here's your reason.

497
00:26:12,530 --> 00:26:20,360
You got the selling imbalance. You're seeing these ratios here to hide behind.

498
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:26,300
You know, if you're getting short in this area, you know, you get a nice little move lower.

499
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:37,150
Okay, this one is a little bit more, I'll say esoteric, but it's a GAN fan.

500
00:26:38,390 --> 00:26:41,610
You could Google GAN fans and try to understand them.

501
00:26:42,290 --> 00:26:48,390
But for me, you know, it's the way I view it is it's sort of a fancy trend lines.

502
00:26:48,990 --> 00:26:50,730
It's like an array of trend lines.

503
00:26:50,730 --> 00:26:52,219
But, you know, what

504
00:26:52,219 --> 00:26:55,197
I've always found important with the GAN fans

505
00:26:55,197 --> 00:27:00,409
is the 45-degree line, which is this one in the middle, the 1x1 line.

506
00:27:01,390 --> 00:27:02,730
To me, that's the most important.

507
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:09,150
You know, a lot of people will look at this 2x1 or this 4x1.

508
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:10,617
You know, the

509
00:27:10,617 --> 00:27:11,696
price will hold the 4x1.

510
00:27:11,696 --> 00:27:12,775
The one that fails, it'll

511
00:27:12,775 --> 00:27:15,149
hold the 2x1. The one that fails, it'll hold the 1x1.

512
00:27:15,150 --> 00:27:18,730
But for me, the most important one is I've always found it.

513
00:27:18,850 --> 00:27:21,790
And I did do a study into GAN stuff

514
00:27:21,790 --> 00:27:24,430
earlier in my career back in the 90s.

515
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:31,950
You know, for me, I've sort of carried the 1x1 line over to my normal trading.

516
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:34,790
You know, it's a level I'm always looking at.

517
00:27:34,870 --> 00:27:36,830
Basically, it's the 45-degree angle line.

518
00:27:37,690 --> 00:27:42,030
And, you know, I'm always interested if we're going to break that, you know, for the breakdown to occur.

519
00:27:42,510 --> 00:27:43,322
You know, and

520
00:27:43,322 --> 00:27:44,405
here I see, you

521
00:27:44,405 --> 00:27:45,488
know, at the 45-degree

522
00:27:45,488 --> 00:27:46,571
line, you know, the

523
00:27:46,571 --> 00:27:49,549
single print bar, you know, with the ratio that I like.

524
00:27:49,670 --> 00:27:50,179
So, you

525
00:27:50,179 --> 00:27:51,198
know, to me, it's

526
00:27:51,198 --> 00:27:52,726
indicating that if we could break

527
00:27:52,726 --> 00:27:54,000
this level, this 45-degree line,

528
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,548
you know, we should stay below it and go lower.

529
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:01,780
But for me now, the

530
00:28:01,780 --> 00:28:03,880
45-degree line, I don't necessarily draw the

531
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:06,880
angles on the chart. It's more of a visual thing.

532
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:17,500
Now, this is the Andrews pitchfork. And it's an interesting tool.

533
00:28:18,180 --> 00:28:18,842
You know,

534
00:28:18,842 --> 00:28:20,167
it's an old-timers, I'll

535
00:28:20,167 --> 00:28:22,155
say old-timers tool, but it's a

536
00:28:22,155 --> 00:28:24,143
tool used by, you know, people

537
00:28:24,143 --> 00:28:28,119
that have sort of been around the markets for a long time.

538
00:28:28,740 --> 00:28:30,380
You sort of see it rehashed nowadays.

539
00:28:31,060 --> 00:28:35,760
But, you know, there's a lot of people that trade eggs followed it back,

540
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:39,380
you know, 20, 30 years ago. But it's still followed today.

541
00:28:39,380 --> 00:28:46,880
And it is, it's an interesting little technical analysis piece.

542
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:51,460
You know, basically, you have a channel here and you're looking for the breakout again

543
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:54,080
of the pitchfork, you know, it's shaped like a pitchfork.

544
00:28:54,620 --> 00:29:00,060
So here, you know, you're inside this, inside this lower channel.

545
00:29:00,460 --> 00:29:02,440
So you're going to be looking for a breakout.

546
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:07,220
And what's the first sign is, okay, maybe we could be close to a breakout.

547
00:29:07,220 --> 00:29:08,400
You have this selling imbalance.

548
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:11,520
So if you could break out through there, you know, where does it go?

549
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:17,640
It sells off nicely down to, you know, you know, basically a four or five point sell-off.

550
00:29:19,520 --> 00:29:24,860
It's, I said, it's, again, it's an indicator that comes with most trading software.

551
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:30,260
You know, I said I use NinjaCator, sorry, NinjaTrader, and it's on there.

552
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:34,420
You know, just you right-click on your chart and you can pull it up.

553
00:29:34,420 --> 00:29:39,140
So, again, this is more on a longer-term chart.

554
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:45,200
And, you know, what you want to see is when you're touching these areas,

555
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:48,380
you know, the channels, how price is reacting.

556
00:29:49,580 --> 00:29:52,820
You know, here you get on the other side of it, but, you know, you got some,

557
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:55,440
you got a ratio, which is bullish.

558
00:29:55,620 --> 00:29:56,880
You know, you trade right back into it.

559
00:29:56,900 --> 00:29:57,562
So, you know,

560
00:29:57,562 --> 00:29:58,445
maybe, you know, you

561
00:29:58,445 --> 00:29:59,549
didn't catch that move, you

562
00:29:59,549 --> 00:30:01,537
know, because it's a little bit on the outside.

563
00:30:01,540 --> 00:30:04,140
I don't necessarily know if I would have been getting short there.

564
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:08,020
You know, if I was, when I see this ratio, I'd be looking to get long again.

565
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:10,840
You know, we're trading up to the middle.

566
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:12,280
I'm not a fan of trading in the middle.

567
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:14,300
Then we start touching it again here.

568
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:17,120
You know, this is around the 46 level.

569
00:30:18,540 --> 00:30:22,320
And you see in ratios, it just trades right back up into it again.

570
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:28,160
So, it's, you know, when you're touching the bottom of a channel, you know, watch what price is doing.

571
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:34,070
Okay, now, this is on a bond.

572
00:30:34,210 --> 00:30:37,150
This is, you know, as the market went down, you got your pitchfork here.

573
00:30:37,690 --> 00:30:42,590
You're trading at the upper end of the channel, and you start to break out.

574
00:30:42,690 --> 00:30:45,270
And what happens right when you break out?

575
00:30:45,430 --> 00:30:47,330
You broke out here, but you traded back inside.

576
00:30:48,010 --> 00:30:51,350
But now it's giving you a sign that it wants to break out again, and you have a ratio.

577
00:30:52,610 --> 00:30:54,550
You know, you got a small print forming there.

578
00:30:54,550 --> 00:30:58,290
And, you know, the market did break out of it, but it went mostly sideways.

579
00:30:59,030 --> 00:31:01,270
I mean, that's a light win.

580
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:05,190
You know, it's, a couple ticks is a couple ticks.

581
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:10,530
You know, it's not every winner is going to be something you can go on vacation with.

582
00:31:10,830 --> 00:31:14,710
But you add enough of them together, then that's great.

583
00:31:15,230 --> 00:31:20,230
So, these are just a few of the great ways you can integrate order flow with traditional technical analysis.

584
00:31:20,790 --> 00:31:24,730
Personally, I'm not one to use many indicators on my charts due to the cluttered feeling it gives me.

585
00:31:25,530 --> 00:31:26,870
And I prefer to keep it simple.

586
00:31:27,350 --> 00:31:29,138
However, I know there are traders killing

587
00:31:29,138 --> 00:31:30,926
it out there that, because they use

588
00:31:30,926 --> 00:31:35,269
order flow in their own technical analysis, and are kept out of a lot of bad trades.

589
00:31:35,770 --> 00:31:38,530
Like I said, you know, say you have your own support and resistance lines,

590
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:42,950
but you notice half the time they work, half the time they don't work.

591
00:31:42,990 --> 00:31:44,288
What you want to do is you

592
00:31:44,288 --> 00:31:45,586
want to refine it and get more

593
00:31:45,586 --> 00:31:48,368
of the times that they do work and less of the times they don't work.

594
00:31:49,550 --> 00:31:52,290
I do think order flows can help you in that regards.

595
00:31:52,970 --> 00:31:55,470
I have customers that came

596
00:31:55,470 --> 00:31:58,970
to me. They wanted to learn order

597
00:31:58,970 --> 00:32:06,470
flow specifically because they know how price reacts around their levels, but sometimes it works,

598
00:32:06,550 --> 00:32:08,473
sometimes it doesn't work, and they

599
00:32:08,473 --> 00:32:11,358
wanted to refine their entry levels or learn to

600
00:32:11,358 --> 00:32:17,128
stay in a trade maybe a little bit longer when the trade is right based on their analysis.

601
00:32:17,450 --> 00:32:18,810
So they'll use it in two ways.

602
00:32:18,870 --> 00:32:20,490
One, they'll use it to refine their entries.

603
00:32:21,230 --> 00:32:24,270
And two, they'll use it to try and get a little bit more out of the trade.

604
00:32:24,590 --> 00:32:26,380
Like I said, if you could add an

605
00:32:26,380 --> 00:32:28,170
extra tick to every trade at the end

606
00:32:28,170 --> 00:32:35,330
of the day, that could add up at the end of a week, at the end of a month, at the end of the year, it could be a lot of money.

607
00:32:36,770 --> 00:32:39,030
And you shouldn't sneeze at one tick.

608
00:32:40,150 --> 00:32:41,436
So I mean, I said, just making

609
00:32:41,436 --> 00:32:42,538
one extra tick, imagine what sort

610
00:32:42,538 --> 00:32:44,008
of difference that could make in the trading.

611
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:51,450
So that's the end of lesson number 18, integrating order flows with traditional technical analysis.

612
00:32:51,990 --> 00:32:53,568
In the next lesson, I'll let you

613
00:32:53,568 --> 00:32:56,949
apply all you've learned via a series of charts in different markets on different days.

614
00:32:57,410 --> 00:32:58,770
So you can see the thinking process

615
00:32:58,770 --> 00:33:04,110
as the day unfolds. This next lesson, lesson 19, is going to be a long one

616
00:33:04,110 --> 00:33:12,250
just because I'm going to show you charts on an intraday basis and sort of let you digest it.

617
00:33:12,330 --> 00:33:13,210
Then I'll discuss it.

618
00:33:13,390 --> 00:33:14,410
So thank you.

619
00:33:14,450 --> 00:33:16,190
That's the end of lesson 18.

